From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 17:55:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: g16: Optionally start render units 0 and 1
 with a small TPC

Render units 0 and 1 of every render VM back a 16 MiB TPC and an 8 MiB
tilemap from their first render, 48 MiB per client, although a desktop
client's renders fit the 1 MiB TPC and tilemap a compact unit has. At
the idle desktop 1.1132 held 563.2 MiB of driver memory for two render
clients.

Add g16_unit_large_lazy (runtime, default 0). When it is set, a VM's
units 0 and 1 are built with a 1 MiB TPC and a 1 MiB tilemap at their
usual addresses. The first render that fits no unit's own set has a
16 MiB TPC and an 8 MiB tilemap built for unit 0 in SUBMIT, before
publication, which unit 0 then keeps for the life of the arena. The
switch is read when a VM builds its first render units: VMs that
already rendered keep the units they have. Nothing changes while it is
0; its stats line is printed only once it was used.

Not yet measured on a device.

Assisted-by: LLM
